    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "`AxNat.bezout m n g` abbreviates the balanced form. The balancing is forced: the naturals have no negatives, so a Bezout coefficient that would be negative is moved to the other side of the equation instead. formal.statement is the type the kernel admitted, taken verbatim from Kernel::render_lean over the environment build_nat_prelude produces; it was not transcribed by hand. The sort renders as `AxNat` (the prelude's own inductive) while declarations are rooted at `Nat`.",
